1gtw|a|Belonging to; belonging exclusively or especially to; peculiar; -- most frequently following a possessive pronoun, as my, our, thy, your, his, her, its, their, in order to emphasize or intensify the idea of property, peculiar interest, or exclusive ownership; as, my own father; my own composition; my own idea; at my own price. ; To hold as property; to have a legal or rightful title to; to be the proprietor or possessor of; to possess; as, to own a house.	j:1izx,75,3;euk,66,60;1l60,59,11;xj8,55,2;767,53,4;1gys,50,4;1a4n,49,6;1tb9,43,8;22r6,40,3;12nk,40,3;fsw,40,2;r0h,39,12;rep,38,6;1o3,36,3;1mhp,36,6~2bbb,17,114;1p0j,8,113;1rdb,20,99;3fx,12,95;1xs2,32,61;euk,66,60;r0e,24,51;2323,16,49;2bb7,34,30;1ffh,26,26;1hhv,1,24;sle,9,23;1cz7,16,21;10aj,24,20;scp,10,20
